-# Release-train divergence fix: relfix-apparently-07240337
-
-**Date:** 2026-07-24
-**Blocked commit:** 9e3bc5b4 ("release-train: refresh orchestrator/dev from origin/master")
-
-## Divergence state
-
-The production push guard blocked commit 9e3bc5b4 because no green
-release-train proof exists for it. Investigation:
-
-- **origin/master** is at 0b78d1db (17 commits ahead of origin/orchestrator/dev)
-- **origin/orchestrator/dev** is at 8f3b4271 (an ancestor of origin/master — 0 commits unique)
-- **local orchestrator/dev** is at 9e3bc5b4, which is a merge commit with
-  parents 21ccea46 and 0b78d1db — this commit exists only locally and was
-  never pushed to origin
-
-## Root cause
-
-A local "release-train: refresh orchestrator/dev from origin/master" merge
-(9e3bc5b4) was created on the local orchestrator/dev branch but never pushed
-to origin. The production push guard then encountered this unpushed commit
-and blocked it because it has no release-train proof on origin.
-
-Meanwhile, origin/master already contains all the content from
-origin/orchestrator/dev (orchestrator/dev is a strict ancestor), so there is
-no actual content divergence — only a local branch pointer that is ahead of
-its remote tracking branch.
-
-## Recommended resolution
-
-1. **Reset local orchestrator/dev** to match origin/orchestrator/dev:
-   `git checkout orchestrator/dev && git reset --hard origin/orchestrator/dev`
-2. The release train can then fast-forward origin/orchestrator/dev to
-   origin/master since orchestrator/dev is already an ancestor.
-3. No merge is needed — this is a pure fast-forward situation.
-
-The unpushed local merge commit (9e3bc5b4) can be safely discarded since all
-its content is already on origin/master.
